##### =====================================================================
##### squid.conf - BAKED-IN DEFAULT, not the runtime config
##### =====================================================================
##### THIS FILE IS A FAIL-CLOSED FALLBACK. The authoritative squid.conf is
##### delivered at boot from OCI Object Storage by
##### /usr/local/bin/fetch-squid-config.sh, sourced from
##### hyperswitch-infra:terraform/catalog/units/oci/squid-proxy/config/
##### squid.conf via the squid-proxy composition module's config bucket.
##### This copy exists so that an instance whose config fetch fails - which
##### is the CURRENT state, because instance principals are not wired up yet
##### (see the composition module README's "Not yet implemented,
##### deliberately: Identity") - still boots a Squid that starts, parses and
##### DENIES EVERYTHING rather than one that either crash-loops or, worse,
##### falls back to Ubuntu's stock config.
#####
##### IT IS DELIBERATELY KEPT BYTE-COMPATIBLE IN BEHAVIOUR with the unit's
##### copy, so that "the fetch worked" and "the fetch did not work" differ
##### only in which domains are allowed, never in the security posture. The
##### allowlist file it reads is created EMPTY by the Packer build, so with
##### no fetched allowlist the effective policy is deny-all.
#####
##### DRIFT WARNING: there are now two copies of this config, one per
##### repository. If you change the unit's copy
##### (hyperswitch-infra:terraform/catalog/units/oci/squid-proxy/config/
##### squid.conf), change this one too, or the fallback posture stops
##### matching the intended one. The alternative - having the image fetch its
##### own default from somewhere - reintroduces the very network dependency
##### this fallback exists to survive.

##### Disable cache - matches the AWS, GCP and OCI unit configs
cache deny all

##### CONNECT (HTTPS tunnel) is only allowed to a small fixed port list, so
##### this proxy cannot be used to tunnel arbitrary TCP to other ports.
##### 443 is the normal HTTPS tunnel port. 587 is kept as a DOCUMENTED
##### exception: the smtp-relay workload tunnels the email relay to OCI Email
##### Delivery over it (control 13f, workplan W2). 80 was removed - a plain
##### HTTP CONNECT is not needed and, with Safe_ports below, is not the way
##### clean HTTP is meant to flow through this proxy.
acl SSL_ports port 443
acl SSL_ports port 587
acl CONNECT method CONNECT
http_access deny CONNECT !SSL_ports

##### HTTP (non-tunnel) egress is restricted to the well-known web ports.
##### Without this a plain HTTP request to an allowlisted domain could be
##### made on ANY port, which is not the posture intended (control 13f).
acl Safe_ports port 80 443
http_access deny !Safe_ports

##### Do not leak client identity into forwarded traffic (control 13f,
##### defence in depth): do not insert our own Via hop, delete the
##### X-Forwarded-For header Squid would otherwise append, and suppress the
##### Squid version banner Squid appends to error pages.
via off
forwarded_for delete
httpd_suppress_version_string on

##### Defence in depth that does not depend on the NSG: only the OKE pod span
##### may proxy through this fleet. 10.90.32.0/20 = the oke-pods subnet
##### (vcn_cidr_prefix 10.90). Decided via the oracle gate (2026-10-09): OCI NLB
##### is is_preserve_source=true, so squid sees the real pod source IP, not the
##### NLB's 10.90.8.17. NPN CNI gives pods their own VNIC IPs in this span,
##### un-SNAT'd to the node. The node subnet 10.90.16.0/20 is deliberately NOT
##### added: the NSG layer already authorizes only pod-subnet clients to the NLB
##### (no worker-nsg rule near squid), so a pods-only ACL is consistent with -
##### not a widening of - the NSG. Health probes are bare TCP connects and never
##### reach http_access, so they are not blocked.
acl oke_pods src 10.90.32.0/20

##### Domain allowlist. Written by /usr/local/bin/update-squid-whitelist.sh
##### from the allowlist object in Object Storage, on a 15-minute cron. The
##### Packer build creates this file EMPTY, so an instance that never
##### successfully fetches an allowlist permits nothing.
acl allowed_sites_domain dstdomain "/etc/squid/squid.allowed.sites.txt"

##### Allow only pod-subnet clients to the allowlisted domains. First-match
##### wins in Squid: the CONNECT port restriction is evaluated before this.
http_access allow oke_pods allowed_sites_domain

##### Deny everything else
http_access deny all

##### Must match the unit's squid_port input and the NLB listener port.
http_port 0.0.0.0:3128

##### W3 (control 13c): Squid runs as user/group `proxy` via a systemd
##### drop-in. The master process still needs to write the pid file, so the
##### pid lives under systemd's RuntimeDirectory=/run/squid, owned proxy:proxy.
pid_filename /run/squid/squid.pid

coredump_dir /var/spool/squid